# What the image build does not need.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` sends the whole working tree to the daemon — the git
# history, a coverage profile that is several megabytes, the accessibility
# screenshots, and the design prototype. None of it reaches the binary, but all of
# it is transferred on every build and any change to any of it invalidates the
# layer cache. A rebuild after running `make cover` would miss the cache entirely.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Test and audit output.
.coverage
.a11y-shots
coverage.out
*.test

# The design source of truth, which is half a megabyte and not part of the
# product. See docs/design-walkthrough.md.
index.html

# The browser accessibility suite: its own module, needs a Chrome, and cannot be
# reached from the binary.
test

# Build output that would otherwise be copied in and then overwritten.
whitelabel-dpi-dashboard
whitelabel-dpi-dashboard-*

# Documentation and local compose files.
docs
README.md
LICENSE
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
